-˙What is ISO13399?
-ISO13399 is an international standard for the purpose of standardizing the electronic data of tools in the world.
-˙Switching to the dimension symbols conforming to ISO13399
-In this catalog, we use the dimension symbols (properties) conforming to ISO13399 international standard.
-Below are the examples of the change.
-˙Examples of the change:
-Before After
-Insert
-Turning
-Milling
-Drilling
-ISO13399 standardizes not only the format of 2D and 3D CAD data but also the tool dimension symbols (properties) and reference position 
-information. This allows the tool information to be read and combined into NC programs and CAM software, regardless of any tool  maker's 
-data. In addition to General Catalog (paper catalog), we are also  updating the symbols in e-catalog (electronic catalog on our website) to 
-the properties conforming to ISO13399. The e-catalog also provides 2D and 3D CAD data in accordance with ISO13399 standard.
